Interpretation
  The densest 3-point factor is K3, but K3 has no norm-t displacement with t>1,
  so it is resonance-free. The 3-point factors that do carry a transverse
  displacement lose an internal edge; even their best bonus against all 9-patches
  does not recover the K3 generic budget. The first small factor that can be both
  edge-dense and norm-3-bearing is size 4, and 4x7 is exactly the Moser crossing.

